      "worked_solution": "We will graph each branch separately.\n\n- On the interval $(-\\infty ,3],$ we have a line with a slope of $\\frac{1}{3}$ and $y$-intercept $0.$ So the graph is the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x$ that ends at $(3,1),$ including this point.\n\n- On the interval $(3,\\infty ),$ we have a horizontal line that passes through the point $(3,2).$ So the graph is the line $y=2$ that starts at $(3,2),$ excluding this point.\n\nTherefore, the function is defined as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}x,\\, & x\\le 3 \\\\ 2,\\, & x>3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
